      <div type="clause" n="21">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 21</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="21" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="324" ed="#liebermann"/>Ac<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#IICn_21.lnote.oe.star"/> we wyllað, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc man ofer XIIwintre<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_21.lnote.oe.2-3"/> sylle þone<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_21.lnote.oe.3-2"/> að, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he nelle þeof beon ne þeofes gewita.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="21" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="324" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ðeofan. We wyllað, þæt ælc man ofer twelfwintre sylle [þo]ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_21.lnote.oe.1"/> að, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he nyle ðeof beon ne ðeofes gewita.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="21" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="324" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ we wyllað, þæt ælc man ofer twelfwintre sylle þonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_21.lnote.oe.2-4"/> að, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he nelle þeof beon ne ðeofes gewita.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="21" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="325" ed="#liebermann"/>Uolumus, ut omnis homo post XII. etatis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_21.lnote.oe.2-2"/> suę annum iuret, quod<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_21.lnote.oe.3"/> fur esse nolit nec furi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_21.lnote.oe.4"/> consentaneus.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="21" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="325" ed="#liebermann"/>Propterea pręcipimus, ut omnis homo ultra (ętatem<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_21.lnote.oe.3-3"/>) duodecim annorum faciat sacramentum, quod nec latro uult esse nec latroni<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_21.lnote.oe.4-2"/> consentire.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="21" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="325" ed="#liebermann"/>Et uolumus, ut omnis homo duodennis iuret, quod numquam erit fur uel furis conscius (iuramento abrenunciet furto uel furti conscientie).</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="21" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="184" ed="#robertson"/>Be ðeofan. We<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#IICn_21.robnote.fn.9"/> wyllað þæt ælc man ofer twelfwintre sylle þone<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#IICn_21.robnote.fn.10"/> að, þæt he nyle ðeof beon ne ðeofes gewita.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="264" ed="#rabin-doml"/>Ac we wyllað þæt ælc man ofer XII wintre sylle þone að þæt he nelle þeof beon ne þeofes gewita.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="324" ed="#liebermann"/>(Von Dieben. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Und (Aber <hi rend="italic">G</hi>) wir wollen, dass<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_21.lnote.de.1"/> jeder mehr als zwölfjährige<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_21.lnote.de.2"/> Mann folgenden Eid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IICn_21.lnote.de.3"/> leiste: dass er weder Dieb noch Diebes Mitwisser<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IICn_21.lnote.de.4"/> sein wolle.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of thieves. B) And (But, G) we will that every man over twelve years old swear this oath: that he will be neither a thief nor an accessory to a thief.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="185" ed="#robertson"/>Concerning thieves. It is our desire that everyone, over twelve years of age, shall take an oath that he will not be a thief or a thief's accomplice.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="464" ed="#whitelock"/>And it is our will that every man over twelve years of age is to give an oath that he will not be a thief or accessory to a theft.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="265" ed="#rabin-doml"/>But we desire that each person over the age of twelve give their oath that they will be neither a thief nor a thief’s accomplice.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">G's ‘Ac’ is perhaps wrongly taken from the beginning of the previous sentence. B's heading is red. Liebermann compares the Instituta 7 and Ld.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 325, October 2026 (MS Cons); AV: corrected against Rabin p. 264 / 265, October 2026 (was “thief ’s”, now “thief’s”)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">B adds rubric Be ðeofan</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">Ac: omitted B; And A</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_21.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">iu. — conscius <hi rend="italic">nur Hk</hi> [<hi rend="italic">offenbar frühere, durch</hi> iuram. — conscientie <hi rend="italic">zu ersetzende Lesung</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">iu. — conscius only Hk [evidently an earlier reading, to be replaced by iuram. — conscientie]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_21.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">þo <hi rend="italic">neu auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">þo written anew on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_21.lnote.oe.2-2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">s. e. <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">s. e. K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_21.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ipse <hi rend="italic">fügt zu K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ipse added by K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_21.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_21.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">irrig aus Beginn vorigen Satzes? Vgl. Inst.</hi> ⁊ <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">in error from the beginning of the previous sentence? Cf. Inst. ⁊ Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_21.lnote.oe.2-3" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">twelfw. <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">twelfw. Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_21.lnote.oe.3-2" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðonne <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðonne Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_21.lnote.oe.2-4" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">324</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. o.</hi> 15, 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. above 15, 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_21.lnote.oe.3-3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_21.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">325</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nem <hi rend="italic">Cb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nem Cb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_21.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl Gl</hi> Ehrlichkeitsversprechen 4a. b; Mitwissen 6</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf Gl</hi> Ehrlichkeitsversprechen 4a. b; Mitwissen 6</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_21.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. o</hi>. 20⁴</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. above</hi> 20⁴</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_21.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Diesen Eid, aus Inst, legt Bracton f. 124b Edward dem Bek. bei. Ähnlichen schwur man unter Heinrich I. (Hn 30) und II. <hi rend="italic">Vgl</hi>. Kemble <hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> II 35; Stubbs <hi rend="italic">Constit. hist</hi>. I 206. 507. 515</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This oath, taken from Inst, is attributed by Bracton f. 124b to Edward the Conf. A similar oath was sworn under Henry I (Hn 30) and Henry II. <hi rend="italic">Cf</hi>. Kemble <hi rend="italic">Saxons</hi> II 35; Stubbs <hi rend="italic">Constit. hist</hi>. I 206. 507. 515</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_21.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">205</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Gegen Begünstigung (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 2. 20) <hi rend="italic">vgl</hi>. Cn 1020, 12</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Against harbouring (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 2. 20) <hi rend="italic">cf</hi>. Cn 1020, 12</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_21.robnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">184</biblScope></bibl><label>We</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">Ac we</hi> G; ⁊ <hi rend="italic">we</hi> A.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_21.robnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">184</biblScope></bibl><label>þone</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þonne</hi> (<hi rend="italic">ð-</hi>) A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
